The train's speed is 48 km/hr. To convert to meters per second, we multiply by (1000 m//cl) and (1/36 s/h):

Speed of train in m//cl. s = 45 km/hr * (1000 m/cl) * (1/36 s/h) = 45 * 1000 / 36 m/sec = 1250/9 m/sec

The train is 150 m ahead of the jogger.

The train takes 25 seconds to pass the jogger. This means that the train covers the distance of the distance between the train and the jogger (150 m) plus the length of the train in 25 seconds.

The relative speed of the train with respect to the jogger is the difference between their speeds:

Relative speed = speed of train - speed of jogger = (1250/9) m/sec - (250/9) m/sec = 1000/9 m/sec

The train takes 25 seconds to pass the jogger, so the total distance covered by the train relative to the jogger is the length of the train plus the initial distance between them.

