\[
\int_{0}^{1}\left(3 e^{x}+2 \sqrt{x}\right) d x = \left[ 3 e^{x} + \frac{2}{3} x^{3/2} \right]_{0}^{1} = \left( 3 e^{1} + \frac{2}{3} \cdot 1^{3/2} \right) - \left( 3 e^{0} + \frac{2}{3} \cdot 0^{3/2} \right) = \left( 3 e + \frac{2}{3} \right) - (3 + 0) = 3 e + \frac{2}{3} - 3 = 3 e - \frac{7}{3}.
