","First, let's convert the speeds of the jogger and the train to meters per second.

The jogger's speed is 9 km/hr. To convert to meters per second, we multiply by (1000 m/km) and (1/36 s/h):

Speed of jogger in m/s = 9 km/hr * (1000 m/km) * (1/36 s/h) = 9 * 1000 / 36 m/s = 250/9 m/s

The train's speed is 48 km/hr. To convert to meters per second, we multiply by (1000 m//cl) and (1/36 s/h):

Speed of train in m//cl. s = 45 km/hr * (1000 m/cl) * (1/36 s/h) = 45 * 1000 / 36 m/sec = 1250/9 m/sec

The train is 150 m ahead of the jogger.

