","To derive the expression for the square root of the momentum tensor \( Q^2 \), we start with the definition of the momentum tensor \( Q \):

\[
Q = P_f - P_i = \left( \frac{E_f}{c}, \mathbf{p}_f \right) - \left( \frac{E_i}{c}, \mathbf{p}_i \right) = \left( \frac{E_f}{c} - \frac{E_i}{c}, \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right).
\]

Now, we calculate \( Q^2 \):

\[
Q^2 = (Q_x)^2 + (Q_x)^2 + (Q_z)^2,
\]

where \( Q_x = \frac{E_f}{c} - \frac{E_i}{c} \) and \( Q_y = \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \).

Substituting the components:

\[
Q^2 = \left( \frac{E_f}{c} - \frac{E_i}{c} \right)^2 + (p_f - p_i)^2.
\]

